# Python style

`from __future__ import annotations`. Ruff: line 100, `E,W,F,I,C4,B,UP` (ignore E501, B008). mypy: `check_untyped_defs`, `no_implicit_optional`, `strict_equality`; `src/` on `mypy_path`.

**Dataclass truthiness**: instances are always truthy. `if not source:` on `DocumentSource` never catches missing data — use `is None` or check fields (`source.id`). Same for other `@dataclass` models.

**Async**: no blocking I/O in async functions. LLM clients and tools are concurrency-safe singletons. ContextVars (`RequestContext`, `UsageMeter`, deadline) copy into asyncio tasks.

**Errors**: subclass `core.exceptions` (`AppError` → Domain / Infrastructure / AI, or `httpx.py` `NotFoundError` / `ForbiddenError` / `ConflictError`). `error_code` is `SCREAMING_SNAKE`. Routes do not build error bodies. 5xx messages stay internal unless `expose_message = True`.

**Logging**: `get_logger(__name__)`. Log types/ids/lengths, never raw queries or document text (`HybridRetriever._warn_degraded`). Prefer `log.exception` in `except`.
